# The guard scene, which F7 in mygame cycles to (see docs/ai/README.md#the-sample): two rooms joined by a doorway, a
# ramp up to a platform in the east room, low cover and tall cover, and a navigation volume over it all. The player, the
# intruder, walks with W, A, S and D, and makes footstep noises; E throws a stone, whose knock is a loud noise. The
# guard, a fox, runs a behavior tree (ai/guard.decision): it patrols between random points, chases the player when it
# sees them, searches where it last saw or heard them, goes to a noise, and barks when it is close. H swaps it to an
# HTN (ai/guard_htn.decision) with the same blackboard and actions. The wary one on the platform runs a utility
# decision (ai/wary.decision) over them too, which weighs chasing, keeping its distance and fleeing by its health,
# which a stone lowers, and its distance to the player. G adds 18 guards, which makes twenty agents. Select an agent in
# the editor while the game plays to see its decision run (see docs/editor/decision-editor.md#live-view). Positions are
# raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m, so 2516582400000000000 is 1.5e11 m. The editor writes this file; see
# docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
